  "title": "Nancy Grace Roman Space Telescope Launches",
  "summary": "NASA’s Nancy Grace Roman Space Telescope, a $4.3 billion dark energy-hunting space telescope, has successfully launched from Florida, marking the start of a three-month mission to explore the universe’s darkest secrets.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The mission launched at 7:26 a.m. EDT Sunday aboard a SpaceX Falcon Heavy rocket from Launch Complex 39A.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The telescope is expected to reach its final orbit in three months and will soon reveal the universe’s darkest secrets.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The mission is part of NASA’s ongoing exploration of the universe, with a focus on dark energy and exoplanet research.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
